```

This solution uses a depth-first search (DFS) approach to explore all possible paths of length `k` starting from each cell in the grid. It keeps track of the current path and updates the minimum path found so far. The `is_valid` function checks if the next cell is within the grid boundaries. The DFS function returns the current path if it reaches the desired length `k`. Finally, the paths are sorted lexicographically and the first path in the sorted list is returned as the minimum path of length `k`.

